(footprint "H11L1"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "kicad-footprint-generator")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Everlight/Vishay/onsemi H11L1 Schmitt-trigger phototransistor optocoupler, 6-lead 300mil DIP (U3, power_in.zcd_opto). This footprint is the real Package_DIP:DIP-6_W7.62mm.kicad_mod land pattern (row spacing 7.62mm/300mil, 1.6mm pads, 0.8mm drill) with a creepage slot added -- pad positions/sizes/nets are otherwise untouched from that verified real footprint. CREEPAGE SLOT, PD3-RETARGETED (docs/evidence/2026-07-28-pd3-retarget-slots.md, superseding the original 8.0mm/5.0x9.0mm design in docs/evidence/2026-07-28-isolator-creepage-slots.md): the entire 6.02mm HV<->SELV gap (pin1/2 at local x=0 vs pin4/5/6 at local x=7.62, inner pad edges at x=0.8 and x=6.82) sits under this DIP package's own moulded body (F.Fab outline x=[0.635,6.985] y=[-1.27,6.35] -- a standard DIP body straddles the gap between its two pin rows), so a post-assembly conformal coating cannot reach it (see docs/evidence/2026-07-28-conformal-coating-pd1.md) but a routed slot -- present in the bare board before the part is ever placed -- can. A 5.0x14.0mm through-board routed slot (Edge.Cuts polygon below, x=[1.3,6.3] y=[-4.5,9.5]) forces the shortest surface path to detour around the slot's end rather than crossing straight across, per IS 15382 (Part 1):2003 = IEC 60664-1 (2002) cl. 4.2 Example 2 (a groove/slot of width >= dimension X is followed along its contour, not bridged; X minimum value = 1.0mm at pollution degree 2, **1.5mm at pollution degree 3** -- re-fetched and independently re-verified against the same primary source this session, docs/evidence/2026-07-28-pd3-retarget-slots.md Sec 1; both PD2 and PD3 X-minimums are exceeded 3.3-5x by this slot's 5.0mm width, so the groove-width floor is not binding at either pollution degree). This part sits far from any board edge or neighbouring copper on the real board (>100mm and ~9.4mm respectively even after the Y-extension), so no placement-driven size cap applies here the way it does for U7. Computationally verified (visibility-graph shortest path around the slot, all 6 HV<->SELV pad-edge pairs): governing creepage = 14.058mm nominal (>= 12.6mm PD3 reinforced-creepage target, 1.458mm/11.6% margin), 13.317mm under worst-case JLCPCB regular-precision slot tolerance (+/-0.2mm/edge, still >= 12.6mm, 5.7% margin). This design also still clears the superseded 8.0mm/PD2 figure with even larger margin. Slot-to-pad copper clearance 0.500mm (HV side) / 0.520mm (SELV side) nominal, 0.300mm/0.320mm worst-case (>= JLCPCB's 0.2mm minimum copper-to-routed-slot clearance; unchanged from the superseded 8.0mm design because the slot's X-extent, which sets this figure, was not touched -- only Y was extended for PD3. Note this worst-case direction is the opposite of the creepage worst-case below: pad-clearance worst-case models each X edge shifting 0.2mm TOWARD its adjacent pad; creepage worst-case below models all 4 edges shrinking the slot -- two independent fab-tolerance failure modes, not one figure reused for both). Slot does NOT extend clearance (through-air line-of-sight distance is unchanged by a surface-level groove/slot per the same standard) -- creepage only.")
	(tags "THT DIP DIL PDIP 2.54mm 7.62mm 300mil H11L1 isolated")
